Error [E0406]: `Result<T, E>` is old Jet error syntax
  --> tests/ui/result_old_syntax.jet:5:11
    |
  5 | fn f() => Result<Int, E> {
    |           ^^^^^^
 Why: fallible Jet types use a success type and an error suffix
 Fix: write `T? E!`, `T (E1 | E2)!`, or `!` for the default Err type
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0406
